WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.520
At the end of Game of Thrones season 8 we
are left bitter and dissapointed with Bran

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.610
Satrk,
this Three Eyed Raven, becoming the new King

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.600
of Westeros
and now we have a revelation coming from none

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.700
other than the Game of Thrones showrunners,
David Benioff and Dan Weiss, that the books

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.800
will end the same.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.250
Speaking in the audio commentary of the season
8 episode 6 that for some reason is the only

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.250
commentary episode that didn't air on the
Game of Thrones official YouTube channel,

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:40.190
a behind-the-scenes look at filming the finale,
showrunners David Benioff and D.B Weiss dropped

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.230
some huge news about the books.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.670
The showrunners confirm Bran being named king
of Westeros

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.390
is author George R.R. Martin’s planned ending
for his the „A Song of Ice and Fire“ novels.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:54.460
They said that the ending will be the same,
Bran Stark will be the King,

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.980
claiming that George RR Martin revealed it
to them,

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:02.129
and ultimately that is why Bran ended up on
the throne at the very end of the show.

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:19.500
George 

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.600
RR Martin himself had this to say about the
endings of both the show and the books.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.080
''How will it all end?

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.670
I hear people asking.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:27.979
The same ending as the show?

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:28.979
Different?

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:29.979
Well… yes.

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:30.979
And no.

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:31.979
And yes.

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:32.979
And no.

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:33.979
And yes.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:34.979
And no.

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:35.979
And yes.''

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:37.700
Martin then proceeds to make three points:
- D&amp;D only had 8 hours for the final season,

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.399
but he'll have more space.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:43.200
- There's the butterfly effect, with changes
from past seasons affecting this one.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.810
- There are lots of characters in the books
who never made it to the show,

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.829
so that changes the entire storyline quite
a bit.

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:54.620
George RR Martin also said that the 8th and
final season of the HBO hit was “not completely

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.840
faithful”
to the plot he has planned.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.450
“Otherwise, the show would have to run another
five seasons” he said.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.000
What all of this means is that the ending
and fates of most of the key characters will

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.250
be the same,
Dany will descend into madness, Bran will

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.920
become the King,
but it's the journey to this point that will

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.260
be entirely different.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.370
Pacing, buildup, characters, everything up
until the end will be quite different.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:20.280
Before this revelation from D&amp;D came out,
I said in my season 8 episode 6 review video

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.791
that I don’t think the ending is necessarily
bad as in fact it’s how George RR Martin’s

00:02:24.791 --> 00:02:28.920
books will also end as they said multiple
times that the ending will be the same, but

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:33.200
the journey to get there will be quite different,
and the journey is exactly what was so disappointing

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.270
in the show.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:37.810
Dany going mad, Bran becoming the King, and
everything else could have been written so

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.250
that all of this would make sense.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.040
Instead, we got rushed and poorly written
season

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.510
where the ending is nowhere near bittersweet,
only bitter.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:48.050
I have no doubt that George RR Martin will
make all of this make sense,

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.160
and most importantly it won't be rushed.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.709
"Who has a better story than Bran the Broken?"

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:57.760
Tyrion says, and for some reason, everyone
accepts it as a valid argument and they proclaim

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.870
Bran the King.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:02:59.870
Why would they do that?

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.730
He has no better claim than anyone else, he
doesn't even have the best story among them,

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:08.370
and he did nothing of great significance in
the war against the Night King.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.050
More like Bran the Useless.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.450
The reasoning seemed weak, and the lack of
set-up is apparent.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.060
What this shows us is that D&amp;D knew they had
to make Bran the King,

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.280
but had no idea how to make it happen, had
no idea how to write his stories,

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.140
had no idea how to make him one of the most
important characters in the show,

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.180
which is why Bran was not even present throughout
the entire season 5,

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.540
and which is ultimately why the ending was
bad.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.690
They failed to deliver Bran's journey to becoming
the King.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:39.099
To talk about Bran's journey in the books
and how will he become one of the most important

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:42.510
characters, we firstly need to understand
George RR Martin's mind.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:46.690
Every important character and event Martin
writes is based on the actual history,

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:49.040
from real events to myths and legends.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.250
The entire A Song of Ice and Fire is inspired
by the Wars of the Roses, a series of English

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.220
civil wars for control of the throne.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:00.930
The houses and characters from those wars
are what inspired most houses and characters

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.230
in Game of Thrones.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:05.400
Most of the characters have their historical
equivalent.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.830
Some of the most shocking moments in TV history
such as the Red Wedding

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:11.290
has historical parallels as well.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:14.690
Even some of the most epic battles are inspired
by real historical battles

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:20.229
such as the Battle of Blackwater which is
based on the second Arab siege of Constantinopole

00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:24.870
where Greek Fire was used to repel the invaders
as it could remain lit on water,

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.480
just like wildfire was used.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:30.301
So now that we know George RR Martin uses
historical characters, events, myths, and

00:04:30.301 --> 00:04:36.190
legends to inspire his own events and characters,
we need to ask ourselves, on who is Bran Stark

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.190
based.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:41.220
Surely, the most important Martin's character
must be based on someone or something as most

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.340
other things are.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.580
Well, some fans might have guessed it right.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.470
Bran is most likely based on the Fisher King
also known as the Wounded King

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:53.720
because much like Bran, a known warrior wounded
him and he is unable to father next generation

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:58.300
to carry on after his death, which is one
of the main points Bran was chosen, King.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:02.990
To make things even more interesting, in Celtic
mythology the Fisher King is derived from

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:07.560
the figure of Bran the Blessed, and the name
Bran in Welsh is usually translated as crow

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.400
or raven,
which oddly matches with Bran and him being

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.780
the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:16.289
George RR Martin once said that a fan theory
got the ending right

00:05:16.289 --> 00:05:20.210
and few fans became confident that they now
know which one it is.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.970
Bran as The Fisher King.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.760
It's a story in which the king is wounded
and then blessed by divine power.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.850
The Fisher King is the last in a long bloodline
charged with keeping the Holy Grail

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.100
much like Bran is charged by the Three-Eyed
Raven from the very beginning

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.500
by appearing in his dreams as a raven to come
to him,

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.259
become him and keep the power of the Three-Eyed
Raven.

00:05:40.259 --> 00:05:45.200
On his way to the Holy Land to find the Holy
Grail, Fisher King was encountered by Three

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.200
Knights.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:50.600
Bran Stark on his way to find the Three-Eyed
Raven is encountered by three threats as well;

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.490
- firstly by the wildlings where he had to
warg Hodor and the Direwolves to avoid being

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.560
found and killed,
- then he encountered the men of the Night's

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.159
Watch at Craster's Keep
where he was captured but managed to escape

00:06:01.159 --> 00:06:05.770
- and finally, for the third time, he was
encountered by wights in front of the three-eyed

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:10.440
raven's cave who were placed there for one
purpose and it's to prevent him from entering

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.819
it
and becoming the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:06:12.819 --> 00:06:16.729
As I already said, the Fisher King has many
similarities with Bran,

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:20.710
from characters itself to their fates and
journey, and names and nicknames

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:23.470
Bran Stark was always supposed to be the King.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:27.190
He's the only type of monarch George RR Martins
sees fit to rule,

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:31.560
the kind where the king suffers on his journey
and is almost de-humanized for the sake of

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:32.690
his people.

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:36.919
In the show, Bran rules from the Red Keep,
yet the Iron Throne is destroyed.

00:06:36.919 --> 00:06:40.370
In the books, it's most likely that Bran will
rule from Harrenhal,

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.650
and the Great Council where they choose the
King will take place not at the Dragonpit,

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.600
but at Harrenhal.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.540
This makes far more sense in the books given
the significance of Harrenhal's succession

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.680
and lordship.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.530
It was here where the previous Great Council
was held

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:56.750
when all the lords chose and voted for the
Targaryen successor

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.210
when King Jaehaerys l Targaryen wasn't certain
who his successor should be.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:04.330
Harrenhal is located on the shore of the Gods
Eye,

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:06.581
the largest lake where the pact between the
First Men

00:07:06.581 --> 00:07:10.050
and the children of the forest was signed
on the Isle of Faces.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:14.250
Harrenhal is also centrally located, being
in the middle of Westeros,

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.970
so I think Bran will rule from Harrenhall,
not Kings Landing.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.680
One of the big differences George RR Martin
will make that will lead to Bran becoming

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:24.550
the king,
is Bran playing the biggest role in defeating

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:25.730
White Walkers.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:29.240
The Long Night was not really long in the
show, it lasted only one night.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.750
Bran Stark didn't showcase any of his powers.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.750
Have no doubt, the books will deliver on the
horrors that were set up,

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:38.639
and the White Walkers won't be defeated in
a single night.

00:07:38.639 --> 00:07:42.860
The Long Night in the books is the event that
will completely change everything.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:46.910
The Others, the Dragons, Greenseers and Skinchangers,
Red Priests,

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:51.610
Faceless Men and undead of all types... we
will see them all play a big role.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.430
How will it lead to Bran the Broken?

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:58.190
Well, Bran will play the biggest role in defeating
the White Walkers, and I believe that will

00:07:58.190 --> 00:07:59.570
win him the throne.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:02.960
There is one interesting quote Stannis gives
to Jon Snow in the books.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.530
Stannis says: ''Lord Seaworth is a man of
humble birth,

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:10.340
but he reminded me of my duty when all I could
think of was my rights.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.940
I had the cart before the horse, Davos said.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.590
I was trying to win the throne to save the
kingdom,

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.740
when I should have been trying to save the
kingdom to win the throne.''

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:23.560
George RR Martin did set this logic of true
King being the one who saves his people,

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.150
and what better king than Bran who saves the
realm from the Long Night.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.539
After the War for the Dawn, people will look
at those who saved them as their new leaders.

00:08:31.539 --> 00:08:35.530
I believe Dany will descend into madness and
die, but the books will do it much better

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:36.750
than the show did.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.349
I believe Jon, who will be another hero of
the Long night,

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:41.930
will be offered to be the King on the Great
Council

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:45.980
on the grounds of him being, not only a hero
but the one with the best claim,

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:50.140
but he will refuse just like his great-great-uncle
Aemon Targaryen did,

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:53.899
and will go far north removing himself from
political court.

00:08:53.899 --> 00:08:57.230
The only and the most important hero left
will be Bran the Broken

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.680
and he will be chosen the King after a long
council.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:04.560
All in all, I believe the books will make
Bran's journey to becoming the king satisfying

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.360
and more importantly, I believe there will
be clues and hints pointing towards it,

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:13.230
while the show gave us only a few that most
of viewers probably didn't even notice.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:16.760
One particular moment in the pilot seems significant
in retrospect.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:21.900
The camera cuts to young Bran during Ned Stark's
recitation of the execution oath.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.230
Just as Ned says the line, ''In the name of
Robert of the House Baratheon,

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:28.630
the First of His Name, King of the Andals
and the First Men...''

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.790
Camera cuts to Bran whom Jon tells not to
look away.

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:36.610
It seems they left it purposely unclear whether
we should focus on Bran or Jon in that shot.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:39.860
That's a tactic the show often uses to subvert
our expectations.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:44.240
For example, after Hardhome, it seemed that
the Night King was after Jon,

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.810
when in fact it was Bran that he really wanted.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:51.890
It seems significant that Bran is also the
first person we see targeted by Jaime Lannister,

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:56.790
the man infamously known as 'Kingslayer.',
trying to slay this King before he even becomes

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:57.790
one.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:01.910
Tyrion approaches Bran in season 8 episode
4 at the victory celebration following the

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.290
Battle of Winterfell.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:07.100
He compliments Bran's wheelchair,
saying it's even better than the saddle he

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.100
designed back in season one.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:13.480
According to Bran, his chair is based on the
one Daeron Targaryen built for his nephew

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.079
120 years ago.

00:10:15.079 --> 00:10:19.210
Bran is talking about Daeron ll Targaryen
knows as Daeron the Good.

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:23.550
He made the wheelchair for his sister Daenerys
Targaryen’s crippled son.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:26.580
His familiarity with that history impresses
Tyrion,

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.010
who told Joffrey back in season 4 that Daeron's
story

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:32.150
should be required reading for any future
ruler.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:37.519
Quote: "The Lives of the Four Kings," Grand
Maester Kaeth's history of the reigns of Daeron

00:10:37.519 --> 00:10:42.920
the Young Dragon, Baelor the Blessed, Aegon
the Unworthy, and Daeron the Good.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:45.490
A book every king should read.''

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.790
In conclusion, the Game of Thrones showrunners
confirmed that George RR Martin's books will

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:52.160
end the same, especially the Bran becoming
the King part.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:56.040
However, this doesn't mean we will be left
bitter and disappointed.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:00.050
Just because the show failed to deliver a
satisfying journey towards this ending.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:03.339
Dany going mad, Bran becoming the King, and
everything else could have been written

00:11:03.339 --> 00:11:07.850
so that all of this would make sense instead
of being rushed, poorly written and bitter.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:12.491
I have no doubt that George RR Martin will
make all of this make sense, give Bran Stark

00:11:12.491 --> 00:11:15.720
a good story,
a good journey and make him useful and make

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.260
him the most important character in the Long
Night.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:21.490
I believe we will get a satisfying and bittersweet
ending in the books,

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:32.519
and I really look forward to Bran Stark's
story.

